# WannaCry (12 May 2017). A worm: it arrived over the network (SMBv1, EternalBlue), with no click from the victim.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee is a hospital clinic receptionist who confirms clinic lists, then the worm arrives mid-shift.
# Invented victim: in England, dozens of hospital trusts were hit and about 19,000 appointments were cancelled.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | WannaCry arrived over the network with no click: an unpatched Windows file-sharing service let it in.
  | It encrypted the documents, changed the wallpaper, opened its "Wana Decrypt0r" window and demanded bitcoin, then tried to spread to the next machines. In May 2017 it hit dozens of hospital trusts in England and about 19,000 appointments were cancelled. The clinic and the receptionist here are invented.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, clinic receptionist at Northwind Community Hospital. Each afternoon you confirm tomorrow's clinic lists in the booking system, so the nurses can print them.
  | You have confirmed 6 of the 8 lists. Two to go.
  | Your booking sign-in is in a text file on the desktop, and so is the patient list for tomorrow. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 6 8 Clinic lists confirmed

# Dana's desk: soft flags, careless but only here to keep the training simple.
file Desktop/booking-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Northwind Clinic Bookings
  | User ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Clinic-2026!
file Desktop/clinic-patients.csv
  at 930 300
  | Clinic,Time,Patient,Phone
  | Cardiology,09:00,Hannah Brooks,555 0142
  | Cardiology,09:20,Omar Haddad,555 0177
  | Orthopaedics,10:00,Linda Voss,555 0123
  | Orthopaedics,10:20,Peter Nkemelu,555 0188

# The two lists. Cardiology goes through the booking system; Orthopaedics is the Word file the clinic still keeps.
file Documents/Clinic list - Orthopaedics.docx
  | Orthopaedics clinic, tomorrow, Room 2
  | 10:00 Linda Voss, knee review
  | 10:20 Peter Nkemelu, hip follow-up
  | 10:40 Grace Mwangi, cast removal
file Documents/Clinic list - Cardiology.docx
  | Cardiology clinic, tomorrow, Room 3
  | 09:00 Hannah Brooks, heart check
  | 09:20 Omar Haddad, blood pressure review

# The booking system: a sign-in page and the Cardiology list behind it.
page clinic-login bookings.northwind.example/clinics/sign-in
  title Northwind Clinic Bookings: sign in
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  favorite
  heading Sign in to Clinic Bookings
  | Welcome back. Sign in to confirm tomorrow's clinic lists.
  field User ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Clinic-2026!
  button Sign in
page list-done bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/confirmed
  title List confirmed
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  heading List confirmed
  | Tomorrow's Cardiology list was sent to Ward 4 for printing.
page list-held bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/held
  title List on hold
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  heading List on hold
  | Tomorrow's Cardiology list is on hold. The ward will not print it until you confirm it.
page list-cardio bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/cardiology
  title Confirm clinic list: Cardiology
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  requires clinic-login
  heading Confirm clinic list: Cardiology
  | A clinic list is waiting for your confirmation.
  section Clinic list
  row Clinic = Cardiology, Room 3
  row Day = Tomorrow
  row Patients booked = 18
  row Send to = Ward 4 printer
  button Confirm and send -> list-done
  button Hold this list -> list-held

mail mail-cardio
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Cardiology list for tomorrow: please confirm
  link list-cardio
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Cardiology's list for tomorrow is ready in the booking system. The link opens it.
  |
  | Priya

step List 7 of 8
  look Mail: Priya's message with the booking link
  | A new list has come in from Priya. This one is a normal one. Confirm it the usual way, so you know what a normal afternoon looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Cardiology list for tomorrow: please confirm

step The link goes to the booking system
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-cardio
  | The email links to the hospital's own booking address, bookings.northwind.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-cardio

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: User ID and Password
  when visit list-cardio
  move Copy the details from booking-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The booking system asks you to sign in first. Two boxes, as on every visit.
open list-cardio

step Check, then confirm
  look the clinic, the day and the number of patients
  when choose clinic-login 1
  | You are in. Check the clinic and the day, then confirm the list or hold it.
signin clinic-login

# IT's reminder: the fix for the flaw WannaCry used, waiting on this PC.
page it-tonight it.northwind.example/updates/scheduled
  title Restart scheduled
  brand Northwind IT
  heading Restart scheduled
  | Your PC will install the update and restart at 22:00 tonight.
page it-later it.northwind.example/updates/postponed
  title Reminder set
  brand Northwind IT
  heading Reminder set
  | We will remind you again tomorrow at 09:00.
page it-restart it.northwind.example/updates/restart
  title Restart needed: security update
  brand Northwind IT
  heading A security update is waiting on your PC
  | Your PC has a Windows security update it has not installed yet. It needs a restart.
  section Update
  row Update = Security Update for Windows: file-sharing fix
  row Waiting for = 8 weeks
  row Restart takes = about 10 minutes
  button Restart tonight at 22:00 -> it-tonight
  button Remind me tomorrow -> it-later
mail mail-it
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Security update waiting on your PC: restart needed
  link it-restart
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | The security update for your PC has been waiting for 8 weeks. It needs a restart, which takes about 10 minutes. Please pick a time in the link below.
  |
  | Marcus, IT

step 7 of 8 done
  look the counter in the guide: one list left
  when choose list-cardio any
  | Done. One list to go. And a message from IT has just arrived.
choose list-cardio 1
quota +1
update Security Update for Windows: file-sharing fix
  kb KB4012212
  size 12 MB
  status available
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Security update waiting on your PC: restart needed

step A message from IT
  look the sender and the link: both are northwind.example, the hospital's own domain
  when mail mail-it
  cue choice:it-restart-1 link:mail-it mail:mail-it app:mail
  move In Marcus's message, click the link, then choose when to restart.
  | Marcus is in IT, and the link goes to it.northwind.example, the hospital's own IT address. The update has been waiting for 8 weeks, and nothing bad has come of it yet. That is how it feels to put off an update.
open mail-it

step Later, or tonight
  look the two buttons: restart tonight, or remind me tomorrow
  when choose it-restart any
  | The page offers a restart tonight at 22:00, or a reminder tomorrow. Either way, the update installs after this afternoon. Another message has just arrived: the last list.
open it-restart
choose it-restart 2
open it-later

# The last list is a Word file, so there is no booking link: Priya sends the file's name.
mail mail-ortho
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last one: Orthopaedics list for tomorrow
  | Dana,
  |
  | The Orthopaedics list is still the Word file: "Clinic list - Orthopaedics" in Documents. Please check it and send it to Ward 4.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last one: Orthopaedics list for tomorrow

# The worm itself: installed as a Windows service, with no file the user ever sees.
program mssecsvc Microsoft Security Center (2.0) Service
  publisher none
  signed no
  process mssecsvc.exe
  cpu 18
  mem 46
  parent services.exe
  command C:\Windows\mssecsvc.exe -m security
  startup mssecsvc2.0 C:\Windows\mssecsvc.exe -m security
  location HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\mssecsvc2.0

# The ransom window: a red lock icon, no warning, and it opens by itself once the files are locked.
view wana-nopay message
  title Wana Decrypt0r 2.0
  icon error
  | You did not pay or we did not confirm your payment yet.
  | (Training copy: no payment exists here.)
  button OK -> close primary
view wana-nodecrypt message
  title Wana Decrypt0r 2.0
  icon warning
  | Your files are still encrypted. No key exists on this training desktop.
  button OK -> close primary
view wana-ransom ransom
  title Wana Decrypt0r 2.0
  app Wana Decrypt0r 2.0
  bg #f2f2f2
  fg #202020
  accent #b00000
  header #a40000
  size 760x470
  heading Ooops, your files have been encrypted!
  icon lock
  | Your important files are encrypted. Many of your documents, photos, videos and databases are no longer accessible.
  section Payment will be raised on
  timer Time left = 259200
  section Your files will be lost on
  timer Time left = 604800
  section What Happened to My Computer?
  | Your important files were encrypted on this computer. They can be recovered only with the private key, which is kept on a server.
  section Can I Recover My Files?
  | Yes. Send $300 worth of bitcoin to the address below. The price doubles after 3 days, and after 7 days the files are lost for ever.
  section How Do I Pay?
  row Bitcoin address = bc1q-training-example-not-a-real-address
  note Nothing here is real. A training copy: no payment is taken and no key exists.
  button Check Payment -> view:wana-nopay primary
  button Decrypt -> view:wana-nodecrypt
  button Copy -> none
  button About bitcoin -> none
  button How to buy bitcoins? -> none
  button Contact Us -> none

# The encryptor the service drops and starts, and the ransom program it runs.
program tasksche tasksche.exe
  publisher none
  signed no
  process tasksche.exe
  cpu 64
  mem 58
  parent mssecsvc.exe
  command C:\Windows\tasksche.exe /i
program wanadecryptor @WanaDecryptor@.exe
  publisher none
  signed no
  description Wana Decrypt0r 2.0
  process @WanaDecryptor@.exe
  cpu 6
  mem 31
  parent tasksche.exe
  view wana-ransom

# The worm arrives. Nothing in the message is wrong and nothing is clicked: it comes in over the file-sharing port.
step Nothing was clicked
  look the “Connection blocked” banner in the corner, and the new start-up item
  when mail mail-ortho
  move Open {File Explorer|Finder} from the {taskbar|Dock}: Priya asks you to check the Orthopaedics list.
  | Priya's last list of the day is an ordinary message. While you read it, an infected computer on the hospital network reaches this one over file sharing (port 445): the old, unpatched service lets WannaCry in. No email, no download, no click.
  | It installs itself as a service called "Microsoft Security Center (2.0) Service", a name chosen to look harmless. First it checks one web address: if that address answers, it stops. Here nothing answered, so it carried on.
  | The “Connection blocked” banner only means this training desktop has no network. In the real outbreak, a researcher registered that address, which slowed the spread sharply.
open mail-ortho
block killswitch-check.invalid 80
launch mssecsvc

# The encryptor runs as soon as the list is opened in {File Explorer|Finder}: every file in Documents is locked.
step Every file gets a new ending
  look {File Explorer|Finder}: the Documents folder, where every file now ends in .WNCRY
  when open files
  move Double-click “Clinic list - Orthopaedics.docx.WNCRY” in Documents.
  cue file:fs-clinic-list-orthopaedics-52bea499 app:files
  | Every file in Documents gains .WNCRY and will not open.
  | The booking system is on the server, so it still works; the Word list was on this PC.
attack ransomware-encrypt
  | Clinic list - Orthopaedics.docx
  | Clinic list - Cardiology.docx
  | Q3-report.docx
  | budget.xlsx
  | ...and 6 more files in Documents
launch tasksche
encrypt Documents .WNCRY
file Desktop/@Please_Read_Me@.txt
  at 820 200
  | Q:  What's wrong with my files?
  | A:  Ooops, your important files are encrypted.
  |
  | Q:  Is there a way to recover my files?
  | A:  Yes. Send $300 worth of bitcoin to the address shown in the Wana Decrypt0r window.
  |     The price doubles after 3 days. After 7 days the files are lost for ever.
  |
  | (Fictional training copy. Nothing on this desktop is real.)
file Desktop/@WanaDecryptor@.exe
  at 820 300
  program wanadecryptor
  size 245760
open Documents

# The locked list will not open, and the ransom window opens by itself: the next step plays after the trainee's own attempt.
step It will not open: a window opens by itself
  look the Wana Decrypt0r window, the new wallpaper, and the note and program on the desktop
  | The list will not open: the computer says it cannot open the file, because it is locked. Then a Wana Decrypt0r window opens by itself, and the wallpaper turns black.
  | It asks for $300 in bitcoin: the price doubles after 3 days, and after 7 days the files are lost for ever.
launch wanadecryptor
wallpaper #0b0b0b
  | Ooops, your important files are encrypted.
  | If you see this text, but don't see the "Wana Decrypt0r" window,
  | then your antivirus removed the decrypt software
  | or you deleted it from your computer.
  | (Training illustration)

step What is running
  look {Task Manager|Activity Monitor}: mssecsvc.exe, tasksche.exe and @WanaDecryptor@.exe, all with no publisher
  when open taskmanager
  | Three programs the worm started are running. mssecsvc.exe is the service that keeps it going, tasksche.exe is the encryptor, and @WanaDecryptor@.exe is the ransom window's program.
  | None of them has a publisher. While you look, Priya writes again: the Word files are locked on every PC.
open taskmanager

# Back to work: the booking system runs on the hospital's server, not on this PC, so Priya moves the last list there.
page ortho-done bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/confirmed-ortho
  title List confirmed
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  heading List confirmed
  | Tomorrow's Orthopaedics list was sent to Ward 4. The clinics will run on paper while the PCs are down.
page ortho-held bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/held-ortho
  title List on hold
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  heading List on hold
  | Tomorrow's Orthopaedics list is on hold. The ward will not print it until you confirm it.
page list-ortho bookings.northwind.example/clinics/lists/orthopaedics
  title Confirm clinic list: Orthopaedics
  brand Northwind Clinic Bookings
  requires clinic-login
  heading Confirm clinic list: Orthopaedics
  | A clinic list is waiting for your confirmation.
  section Clinic list
  row Clinic = Orthopaedics, Room 2
  row Day = Tomorrow
  row Patients booked = 12
  row Send to = Ward 4 printer
  button Confirm and send -> ortho-done
  button Hold this list -> ortho-held
mail mail-paper
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Orthopaedics list: use the booking system
  link list-ortho
  | Dana,
  |
  | Our Word files are locked on every PC, and IT is on its way. Do not open anything else. I have put the Orthopaedics list in the booking system, which runs on the server and still works. Please confirm it there and the ward will print it.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Orthopaedics list: use the booking system

step Back to work, on the server
  look the message from Priya: the booking system is on the server
  when mail mail-paper
  cue choice:list-ortho-1 link:mail-paper mail:mail-paper app:mail
  move In Priya's message, click the link, then confirm the list.
  | Priya says every PC with the Word files is locked, but the booking system runs on the hospital's server and still works. Her message is a real one.
  | Dana is already signed in, so the list opens straight away. Go on: this is how the clinics kept running.
open mail-paper

step The last list, from the server
  look the counter in the guide: 8 of 8
  when choose list-ortho any
  | Done: 8 of 8 lists are dealt with, and the clinics can print from the server. The Word file and the files on this PC are still locked, and the worm is still looking for the next PCs.
open list-ortho
choose list-ortho 1
open ortho-done
quota +1

step It looks for the next PCs
  look the two “Connection blocked” banners in the corner: 192.0.2.10 and 192.0.2.11, both on port 445
  | The worm tries the same flaw on every machine it can reach, on port 445. A patched machine, or one with the old protocol turned off, is safe.
  | Here those connections are blocked. In the real outbreak, hospitals had no such block: appointments were cancelled and ambulances were sent to other hospitals.
attack network-worm
  | 192.0.2.10
  | 192.0.2.11
  | the next PC
  | the next hospital
block 192.0.2.10 445
block 192.0.2.11 445

flag hard process mssecsvc.exe
  | A service named to look like Windows security, from no known publisher: the worm itself.
flag hard startup mssecsvc2.0
  | The worm set itself to start again after every restart, with no one asking for it.
flag hard process tasksche.exe
  | Started by mssecsvc.exe, no publisher, unsigned: the encryptor.
flag hard file Documents/Clinic list - Orthopaedics.docx.WNCRY
  | The same name, with .WNCRY on the end: the file is locked and will not open.
flag hard view wana-ransom
  | A window that opened by itself, demands bitcoin and counts down: the ransom demand.
flag hard file Desktop/@WanaDecryptor@.exe
  | The ransom program: no publisher, no warning, and it opens the demand by itself.
flag hard file Desktop/@Please_Read_Me@.txt
  | The ransom note the worm leaves beside the locked files.
flag hard notice taskmanager connection blocked
  | Port 445 to other PCs: the worm looking for its next victim.
flag soft file Desktop/booking-login.txt
  | A sign-in in a text file on the desktop: anything that runs on this PC can read it. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/clinic-patients.csv
  | Patient names and phone numbers on the desktop belong on the hospital system, not in a loose file.

lesson
  | Install security updates, even when you are busy: Microsoft had fixed this flaw two months before WannaCry. A restart that takes ten minutes is cheaper than a ward on paper.
  | Turn off old services you do not need (here SMBv1), keep patient files on the hospital system, and keep offline backups: WannaCry also deleted Windows' own shadow copies.
  | This worm needed no click, so do not blame the person at the desk: a patched computer, a network that blocks port 445 between PCs, and offline backups are what stop it.
